    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d8-a1-a4">

                <pb facs="0042" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg32"/>

                <head>A.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-07"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >April</hi> 7, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Wife:</hi> I could not get a chance to write to
                    you before. I did write one letter to you. I hope you got it. Dear Celia, I have
                    shipped in this ship and got <hi rendition="#italic">£</hi>10 bounty, and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">£</hi>4 10<hi rendition="#italic">s</hi>. per month, and
                    I have left you half pay. When you receive this go to Jones’s office and you
                    will receive <hi rendition="#italic">£</hi>10, and he will give you half pay,
                    and ask him how you are going to write to me. Dear Celia, when you get this
                    money start in some kind of business. Give my love to father and mother, Stephen
                    and uncle, and tell them I hope I will be soon home again. I have shipped for
                    the war in my own name. I have not got time to say more, but good-night and God
                    bless you. I remain your ever-loving,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">FRANCIS GLASSBROOK.</p>
                <p>This is the letter marked A, referred to in the annexed affidavit of Cecilia
                    Glassbrook.</p>
                <p>Sworn before me this 24th day of November, 1863.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. BUSHELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
